## Critical Reflection

### What went well?

At the end of this project I became very proud of the character selection menu over the games, having used Copilot to help through out the games, mostly with identifying the more suitable nodes and the maths, and doing something multiplayer for the first times. Having created the selection and that the choices of the player translates into the the games as the play, I became proud of that since it worked through out each game.

Also being able to finish to a suitable quality even despite the short amount of time we had to finished the menu and third game was a very good achievement and it was the thing I was stressed about the most.

### What could be improved or done differently next time?

There are definitely things that I would have done differently regarding the camera and movement of characters since both had to be done manually because I chose the wrong template to start out with, next time the third person template is what I would have chosen.

I think also targeting the pace of the game would have been a good idea because despite everything working and it being a very playable set of games, I think for a party game their should have been a more visual aid to create a faster pace to make it a more chaotic party game.

